.TH READELF 1 "March 2026" "Substrate" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
readelf \- display information about ELF files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B readelf
[\fIoptions\fR] \fIfile\fR...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B readelf
inspects ELF32/ELF64 objects and prints headers, sections, segments, symbols,
relocations, dynamic tags, notes, version data, hash histograms, ARM-specific
metadata, dumps, DWARF summaries, and core-file note information.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-file-header
Display ELF header.
.TP
.B \-l, \-\-program-headers
Display program headers.
.TP
.B \-S, \-\-section-headers
Display section headers.
.TP
.B \-s, \-\-syms, \-\-symbols
Display symbol tables.
.TP
.B \-\-dyn-syms
Display only dynamic symbols.
.TP
.B \-r, \-\-relocs
Display relocation tables.
.TP
.B \-d, \-\-dynamic
Display dynamic section.
.TP
.B \-n, \-\-notes
Display note sections and note segments.
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version-info
Display version sections.
.TP
.B \-I, \-\-histogram
Display hash table statistics.
.TP
.B \-g, \-\-section-groups
Display section groups.
.TP
.B \-u, \-\-unwind
Display ARM unwind information.
.TP
.B \-A, \-\-arch-specific
Display ARM architecture attributes.
.TP
.B \-x \fIsection\fR, \-\-hex-dump=\fIsection\fR
Hex dump section by name or index.
.TP
.B \-p \fIsection\fR, \-\-string-dump=\fIsection\fR
String dump section by name or index.
.TP
.B \-w \fIkind\fR, \-\-debug-dump=\fIkind\fR
Display DWARF debug information kind.
.TP
.B \-c
Display core-file notes (also auto-enabled for ET_CORE).
.TP
.B \-e, \-\-headers
Equivalent to \fB-h -l -S\fR.
.TP
.B \-a, \-\-all
Equivalent to core display set (\fB-h -l -S -s -r -d -V -A -I\fR).
.TP
.B \-W, \-\-wide
Do not truncate selected output fields.
.TP
.B \-t, \-\-section-details
Enable detailed section display mode.
.TP
.B \-C, \-\-demangle
Demangle symbol names.
.TP
.B \-D, \-\-use-dynamic
Use dynamic symbol table when printing symbols.
.TP
.B \-\-sym-base=\fI0|8|10|16\fR
Select symbol value radix.
.TP
.B \-\-print-sysv
Enable SysV-compatible formatting where supported.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Display help.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Display version.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Error (for example, non-ELF input or malformed file).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR elfedit (1),
.BR objdump (1),
.BR nm (1),
.BR elfobj (3)
